          "stats": {
            "trait_name": {
              "value": "Self-Destruct"
            },
            "trait_description": {
              "value": "(arcane, aura, evocation)\n\nWhen a clockwork sphinx is reduced to 0 Hit Points, it collapses and emits a steady ticking sound.\n\nAt the beginning of what would've been its next turn, the sphinx explodes into a 20-foot emanation of shrapnel, dealing 6d10 piercing damage (DC 26 basic Reflex save). An adjacent creature can cancel the self-destruct sequence by succeeding at a DC 26 Thievery check to Disable a Device at any point before the sphinx explodes, but on a critical failure, it explodes immediately."
            },
